Scope — what this license covers (ORIGINAL_PROJECT_ASSETS)
----------------------------------------------------------

Only content the project owner actually owns or has the right to license:

- the bundled pet presentation data under `src/dsh/client/pets/` (mapping
  tables, grade descriptions, speech copy, localized strings) and the
  journey pack data under `src/packs/*/manifest.json`;
- the bundled original artwork and derived art generated from it: pet pose
  sprites, journey scenes/subjects, insignia symbols, expression layers,
  keepsake images, and their build inputs (masters and provenance-tracked
  sources);
- the bundled original written copy (pet speech lines, documentation
  authored for this repository where no other license is stated).

Scope — what this license does NOT cover (THIRD_PARTY / HISTORICAL)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing in this repository is relicensed by the mere presence of the
Apache-2.0 or CC BY 4.0 notices. In particular, the following retain all
rights of their respective owners and are included only for interoperability,
historical record, or audit evidence:

- third-party trademarks, logos, and brands (including any references to
  "DeepSeek", "Pony.ai", or other companies) — no affiliation is claimed;
- third-party works and external interfaces referenced for interoperation
  (for example the DeepSeek Harness and its host-provided UI, including the
  whale/deepseek-pet reference);
- third-party screenshots or interface captures kept inside
  `docs/evidence/**` and historical investigation records;
- materials cited inside provenance records (`PROVENANCE*.json`) that the
  project does not own.

Honesty note on AI-assisted assets
----------------------------------

Parts of the bundled original art were produced with the assistance of
generative AI tools through the owner's recorded offline production route
(see the `PROVENANCE*.json` records and each pet's `license.provenance`
pointer). CC BY 4.0 is granted only to the extent of the rights the project
owner actually holds or can license in these works; no broader or exclusive
rights are claimed.

